EXAMPLE DESC takes the rest of the line or nothing, ABORT_ON_FAIL and EXPECT_FAIL stand alone, MONITOR takes a query, STOP or nothing (PlaytestDslExtensionTests.cs:90; WaitConditionTests.cs:173, :185; Pure/PlayerProfilePreflightTests.cs:85, :205, :263; Runtime/PlaytestParserTests.cs:416, :425; AI/playtest-dsl.md:148, :431, :575, :615)
  SOURCE DESC "check health"
  SOURCE DESC move player to start position
  SOURCE DESC
  SOURCE ABORT_ON_FAIL
  SOURCE EXPECT_FAIL
  SOURCE MONITOR economy
  SOURCE MONITOR Player/Health
  SOURCE MONITOR STOP
  SOURCE MONITOR

EXAMPLE ABORT_ON_FAIL and EXPECT_FAIL refuse a token after them, MONITOR a second token (INTENDED I1); a lower-case verb now reads via CASEFOLD (PT-8/Q22, closes INTENDED I4)
  SOURCE ABORT_ON_FAIL now
  SOURCE EXPECT_FAIL x
  SOURCE ABORT_ON_FAIL # fail fast
  SOURCE MONITOR a b
  SOURCE abort_on_fail
  SOURCE desc hello
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:15
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 2:13
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 3:15
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 4:11

EXAMPLE MONITOR refuses a query with a blank inside [..], written without quotes (INTENDED I8)
  SOURCE MONITOR /[My Obj]/X|C|f
  EXPECT diagnostic DECLARE_SYNTAX at 1:9
